<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Fiery October: Reprisal, 1962</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;The Fiery October&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;This series of scenarios is set on the&amp;nbsp;presumption that the Cuban Missile Crisis turned hot following the shootdown of a U-2 over Cuba on 27 October, 1962. It escalates from a tense&amp;nbsp;non-hostile showdown between the&amp;nbsp;US and Soviet Union&amp;nbsp;to a major global conflict within 48 hours. The primary diversion from real events is the decision by President Kennedy to launch reprisal airstrikes against SAM sites in Cuba in retalliation for the U-2 shootdown. From there, the&amp;nbsp;crisis takes on a life of its own. Each scenario&amp;nbsp;in the&amp;nbsp;series&amp;nbsp;covers a new phase of the conflict and presents the player with a detailed look at the&amp;nbsp;potential power and limitations of&amp;nbsp;the USAF&amp;nbsp;in the early&amp;nbsp;60s. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;U&gt;Scenario Background&lt;/U&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In the wake of the U-2 shootdown on Saturday, October 27, 1962, the Cuban Missile Crisis took a dangerous turn. A plan was in place to launch reprisal strikes against any SAM site in Cuba that attacks a US reconnaissance aircraft. President Kennedy and his advisers debated whether or not to approve the strikes and in the end decided against it. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;As the&amp;nbsp;Blue (US)&amp;nbsp;player you will be transmitted orders&amp;nbsp;for reconnaissance and support missions, as well as the reprisal strikes, and attached missions. &lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
